
  List the jobs wtm's daemon runs, in every repository of the machine (--repo
  narrows to one): a group per worktree with the profile its jobs were started
  under, what crashed first, then what runs, then what ended or never started; a
  runner with the services it starts, and each repository's shared services with
  the worktrees holding them. It works from any directory, changes nothing and
  never starts the daemon.

  Usage:
    wtm-next run ps [flags]

  Examples:
    wtm run ps

    # Only this repository's jobs, as JSON
    wtm run ps --repo . --output json

  Flags:
    -h, --help            help for ps
        --output string   Output format: text or json (default "text")
        --repo string     Only this repository's jobs (a path in it)

  Global Flags:
    -q, --quiet   Silence human output; errors and the exit code are unaffected, and --output json still emits its document

